1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,396
The Plant on the Windowsill.

3
00:00:03,396 --> 00:00:06,323
Mom brings home a small plant in a yellow pot.

4
00:00:06,323 --> 00:00:11,010
We put it by the kitchen window, and Ben immediately gives it a name: Professor Leaf.

5
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:13,646
The professor is quiet but seems friendly.

6
00:00:13,924 --> 00:00:15,905
Has anyone watered it today?

7
00:00:16,132 --> 00:00:18,105
I watered it when we got home.

8
00:00:18,105 --> 00:00:19,334
Why?

9
00:00:19,612 --> 00:00:21,906
I was going to give it a welcome drink.

10
00:00:22,132 --> 00:00:23,990
I was thinking the same thing.

11
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:29,063
Mom moves the watering can back to the shelf before Professor Leaf gets three welcomes in one afternoon.

12
00:00:29,332 --> 00:00:31,232
Let's check the care label.

13
00:00:31,232 --> 00:00:33,951
Different plants need different amounts of water.

14
00:00:33,951 --> 00:00:37,367
This one doesn't need a drink every time someone says hello.

15
00:00:37,636 --> 00:00:39,630
We read the little label together.

16
00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:43,609
Mom shows us how she checks the soil and where to put a saucer under the pot.

17
00:00:43,876 --> 00:00:45,474
We need a schedule.

18
00:00:45,474 --> 00:00:47,859
Important professors have schedules.

19
00:00:48,148 --> 00:00:49,642
I'll write it down.

20
00:00:49,642 --> 00:00:52,944
I make a small card where we can record when the plant was watered.

21
00:00:52,944 --> 00:00:56,058
We also agree to ask Mom before adding any more.

22
00:00:56,332 --> 00:00:57,388
Good.

23
00:00:57,388 --> 00:01:00,294
You can both help, as long as you check first.

24
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,032
The next morning, Ben greets the professor on his way to breakfast.

25
00:01:04,032 --> 00:01:08,824
He looks at the card, puts down the watering can, and gives the plant a tiny bow instead.

26
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:11,396
No drink today, Professor.

27
00:01:11,396 --> 00:01:12,906
Just respect.

28
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:14,903
The leaves don't move.

29
00:01:14,903 --> 00:01:17,403
I think that means the professor approves.

30
00:01:17,403 --> 00:01:21,642
Or maybe he's busy preparing a lecture about why people should stop poking his soil.
